{"site":"douban","sid":"4103447","imdb_id":"tt0137863","imdb_link":"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0137863/","douban_link":"https://movie.douban.com/subject/4103447/","chinese_title":"八响致命枪声","foreign_title":"Kahdeksan surmanluotia","year":"1972","aka":["Eight Deadly Shots","八响致命的枪声","八次致命射击"],"region":["芬兰"],"genre":["剧情"],"language":["芬兰语"],"playdate":[],"episodes":"4","duration":"76分钟","description":"A poor farmer tries to get by, but fails. Blood is shed, not out of malice, but simple desperation. A raw exposé on human degradation and deprivation. A work of Zola-esque violence and grandeur, shown here in its ultra-rare, 5h+ original version. The greatest Finnish film ever.\nPeter von Bagh was always joking that Martin Scorsese's World Cinema Foundation should handle the restoration of this Zola-esque monument, as it was obviously made in a Third World country. And true, it's difficult to imagine that the down-trodden, poverty-stricken, backwoods hole we see here is situated somewhere in 1960s Finland.\nThe real-life story on which Eight Deadly Shots is informally based happened in 1969. In a moment of sheer hopelessness, a certain Tauno Veikko Pasanen shoots four police officers. Tauno is called Pasi here and played by scenario-writer Niskanen himself. Pasi ekes out a meagre living for himself and his family. Times grow increasingly harder. One thing slowly leads to another. In the end, there's blood. A raw, grim, uncompromising, unrelenting, unforgiving and non-consoling masterpiece which will be shown in its five-hour-plus original version. A very, very rare opportunity!","poster":"https://img1.doubanio.com/view/photo/l_ratio_poster/public/p2535290982.jpg","douban_votes":"0","douban_rating":"0.0","imdb_rating_average":"8.2","imdb_votes":"1197","imdb_rating":"8.2 / 10 from 1,197 users","director":[{"name":"米科·尼斯卡宁 Mikko Niskanen","link":"https://www.douban.com/personage/27213991/","role":"导演 Director","avatar":"https://img9.doubanio.com/view/celebrity/m/public/p1